//
// Goal 1 increment W1: the SLIDING-WINDOW (banded causal) FlashAttention row.
//
// Shape is deliberately one the registry already carries as causal-passing --
// 2048x2048, dk/dv 64/64, the full-chip config lqp=256 / num_q_tiles=4 /
// num_heads_per_unroll=2 / num_cascade_stages=4 -- so the only variable
// between this and the existing causal coverage is the mask itself.
//
// W = 512 is a multiple of lkp = 64, so the band's trailing edge lands on a
// chunk boundary and no partial-select generalization is required. (The kernel
// handles a non-aligned W too, but the builder refuses it because nothing has
// validated it on hardware.)
//
// WINDOW= feeds BOTH the kernel's -DWINDOW_LEN and the harness's --window from
// one variable, so the reference and the device cannot be given different
// masks from the command line. If they ever were, the element-wise np.isclose
// check would FAIL in either direction; there is no silent-pass mode.
//
// This is CORRECTNESS-ONLY and buys no speedup: the KV chunk loop bound is a
// static compile-time constant, so a windowed run streams and multiplies every
// (Q tile, KV block) pair exactly as an unwindowed one does and then masks more
// of the result. Any GFLOP/s figure from this recipe is the same convention
// the causal rows use and must not be rescaled by the band ratio.
//
// Its negative control is run_npu2_makefile_peano_causal_window512_negative.lit
// and is NOT optional: full causal is a strict SUPERSET of a window, so a
// windowing implementation that silently degraded to full causal is the most
// likely bug class here. Without the control, a PASS below is consistent with
// nothing having been windowed at all.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_causal_window512
// RUN: cd test_causal_window512
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile run PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR LK=2048 LKP=64 LQ=2048 LQP=256 DK=64 DV=64 NUM_HEADS=32 NUM_KV_HEADS=8 WINDOW=512 EXTRA_PY_FLAGS="--causal" | FileCheck %s
//
// The band line first, so a run that quietly took the unwindowed path is
// visible here rather than inferred from the verdict. Then the comparison's
// own statistics, then the verdict, then the headroom against the 1e-1 ceiling
// -- in the order they are actually printed.
// CHECK: [window] reference band W=512
// CHECK: [precision] Output 0
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [precision] atol_required=
